13
01:01:36,521 --> 01:01:42,521
The film follows three women—Carly (Diaz), Kate (Mann), and Amber (Upton)—who
are all romantically involved with the same man (Coster-Waldau).

14
01:06:20,869 --> 01:06:26,869
After finding out about each other, the trio take their revenge on him.

15
01:11:05,217 --> 01:11:11,217
Development of The Other Woman began in January 2012, when 20th Century Fox hired Stack to write
the script, based on the original idea from the 1996 comedy The First Wives Club.

16
01:15:49,565 --> 01:15:55,565
Casting was done between November 2012 and June 2013.

17
01:20:33,913 --> 01:20:39,913
Filming began on April 29, 2013, in locations including Manhattan, Long Island, the Hamptons, Dockers Waterside
Restaurant on Dune Road in Quogue, and the Bahamas, and it concluded on August 27 that year.

18
01:25:18,260 --> 01:25:24,260
Aaron Zigman composed the score and LBI Productions produced the film.

19
01:30:02,608 --> 01:30:08,608
The film was released on April 25, 2014, in the United States,
and distributed worldwide by 20th Century Fox.

20
01:34:46,956 --> 01:34:52,956
The film received mostly negative reviews from critics, but was a box
office success, grossing $196.7 million worldwide.

21
01:39:31,304 --> 01:39:37,304
The film explores themes of infidelity, revenge, unfaithful
boyfriend, extramarital affair, unfaithful husband.

22
